</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">V-C</span> </span><span id="S5.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Ablation Study (RQ2)</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To systematically evaluate the effectiveness of key MOJOFuzzer components—Prompt Engineering (PE), Fine-Tuned LLM (FT), and the Half-Mutation strategy (HM)—we conducted a controlled ablation study using three critical metrics: Hallucination Rate, Valid Code Rate, and Semantic Correctness. We utilized an automated hallucination detection benchmark inspired by HaluEval to identify hallucinated content, defined as unsupported or fabricated API calls and code structures. Valid Code Rate measures the fraction of syntactically correct and executable test cases, while Semantic Correctness assesses whether the test cases meaningfully exercise intended program functionalities.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE IV: </span>Ablation Study Results for MOJOFuzzer Components</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
